 `ui-conversation` owns target-neutral Conversation assembly and the shared browser shell. It consumes Session Controller `SessionEventLikeEntry` feeds, exposes React-free registries and per-Session bindings through `ctx.uiConversation`, and contributes the `useConversation`, `useInput`, and `inputActions` standard props through `ctx.uiSession`. It also owns the per-session durable image URL cache: `ctx.uiConversation.imageUrl(sessionId, attachment)` resolves one Gateway-authorized browser URL per attachment and revokes it with the Session binding, so every Conversation target shares one `session.attachment` read. Concrete targets such as Chat are separate packages that register their own Definitions, snapshot builders, Views, and renderers.
 
+The optional `windowCommit.isCommitting(viewId)` reads that window coordinator's existing synchronous measure/publish/correct state. It reports false for other windows, released windows and after a failed commit. A mounted reader can use it to avoid a competing automatic correction during publication; it does not schedule work or transfer scroll ownership.
+
 ## Table of Contents
 
 - [Conversation assembly](#conversation-assembly)
@@ -213,3 +215,17 @@ None; Conversation assembly and browser input state do not alter provider-side p
 None.
 
 </details>
+
+QueueDock consumes the optional per-row `queueActions` Session projection. An absent projection or row preserves ordinary Edit, Remove and Steer behavior; a source can disable only the actions its original queue supports. Source adapters supply the real Inbox and route accepted actions to that same queue owner.
+
+A source queue without durable attachment references can retain the original local previews by keeping the matching queued pending submission through body handoff. QueueDock matches its `rpcId` exactly, prefers durable attachment references when present, and never borrows another submission’s previews.
+
+Queue action failures notify the input shell of the exact retained reading binding supplied to the dock. Without a reading occurrence, the normal Session binding remains the owner.
+
+The same `queueActions` projection governs the empty-draft steer-all hint and Cmd/Ctrl+Enter gesture. If any queued row disables Steer, neither is offered. InputHub checks the current capabilities again before dispatching each original queue action, so a capability change cannot leave an active whole-queue shortcut. Typed-draft delivery is unchanged.
+
+A source may also supply `editText` for a row whose input contains attachments or references. QueueDock edits that exact text buffer; the source must preserve every non-text part when applying the original row update. With no `editText`, the ordinary text-only editing rule is unchanged.
+
+Sources may set optional `delivery` (`sending`, `confirming`, `failed`) for an owner-held queue row or a local pending request ID. QueueDock keeps its text/attachments visible with native progress and omits actions while no mutable queued item exists. Clearing the state restores per-row capabilities. Missing source state preserves ordinary DSH pending presentation.
+
+An explicit per-row `steer: true` is final source availability, including continuation of its retained operation while the session is idle. Missing row/projection still uses the ordinary running-session condition. The source validates the original operation and captured turn at action time.
