+## Optional indexed reads
+
+`readPage` and `prepareReadIndex` are optional source-side capabilities. A consumer checks their presence rather than opening a complete log on a cache miss. Page cursors describe only the contiguous body; `context` identifies additional original native dependency events. Caller-provided event and byte budgets cover the complete result. `SessionPageCapacityError` reports `CAPACITY_EXCEEDED` only when one native item and its dependencies cannot fit. Existing handles and execution ownership are unchanged.
